				<description>&lt;p&gt;As you may already know, I am in New York with my company, attending the QCon conference.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/IMG_6542.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/IMG_6542-300x199.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; title=&#34;brooklyn bridge&#34; class=&#34;aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1615&#34; height=&#34;199&#34; width=&#34;300&#34; srcset=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/IMG_6542-300x199.jpg 300w, https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/IMG_6542.jpg 1280w&#34; sizes=&#34;(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Earler today I attended Matt Wynne&amp;rsquo;s presentation at QCon New York. It was one of the best presentations I have seen so far. Especially, since he began as his alter-ego, Darren Workshy.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Darren Workshy, hater of behaviour-driven development. Darren has invented &lt;strong&gt;Mortgage-driven development (MDD)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
